07:11.017 --> 07:19.202
[SPEAKER_01]: fundraising, so much. And it was incredibly enjoyable. I learned so much about my country, so much that I realized I don't have to stay in

07:19.242 --> 07:26.247
[SPEAKER_01]: Toronto anymore where I was born and grew up. I could live anywhere. There's nice people everywhere. I don't have to be afraid. I learned so

07:26.287 --> 07:35.393
[SPEAKER_01]: much from that baby of a baby. And so these ideas that somehow seem like they've come out of left field, that it's always just a matter of boiling

07:35.493 --> 07:43.719
[SPEAKER_01]: the big idea down and getting rid of all of that. Okay, I can't do that. Can't do that. Can't do that. Can't do that. Okay, well, what's left? And

07:43.759 --> 07:55.046
[SPEAKER_01]: so what's left is what I would focus on. And then not ironically, I can't think of the word, but organically a project like that, for instance,

07:55.066 --> 08:03.752
[SPEAKER_01]: skateboarding across Canada, that would give me the skills that I needed to then move to the next step and experience that baby's parent,

08:03.832 --> 08:11.137
[SPEAKER_01]: which was powered paragliding across Canada, right? And then from that point, so on and so forth, now we're free flying across the United

08:11.177 --> 08:19.162
[SPEAKER_01]: States. That sounds so interesting. And like hearing you talk about how you made it all happen is basically you structured it very well, like

08:19.222 --> 08:26.726
[SPEAKER_00]: reproduction of ideas eventually coming down to knowing your reality and what is possible and then going for it. But this kind of makes me

