18:42.105 --> 18:49.030
[SPEAKER_01]: recognize, Hey, if I get done with this quick, then I can do whatever I want. I can start editing sooner. I could go on another trip. I could go

18:49.070 --> 19:02.334
[SPEAKER_01]: hang out with my friends. I go to the beach, but give myself that extra few weeks, few months, whatever it is to be able to finish and Incredibly, if

19:02.394 --> 19:13.038
[SPEAKER_01]: I look back on all of my projects, I've never finished early. I almost always finish at the maximum amount of time that I had, regardless of the

19:13.078 --> 19:21.361
[SPEAKER_01]: circumstance. And so that's how important it is for me to have carved out all of that time that may seem unreasonable from the get-go in terms of

19:21.401 --> 19:32.268
[SPEAKER_01]: being able to finish a project, but also finish it, and sorry, finish the project, but also enjoy that journey that i'm not stressing out over am i

19:32.409 --> 19:40.119
[SPEAKER_01]: even going to finish this meanwhile i'm trying to get to canada i'm still in arizona i don't have to stress out about that it took me two months to

19:40.159 --> 19:48.404
[SPEAKER_01]: fly across arizona when i was only budgeting for a month for each state because I'd given myself an extra month. And so I used it there, right?

19:48.604 --> 19:57.649
[SPEAKER_01]: Just, sorry, not to jump ahead, but I think that's an important part is just to really cut some slack, let the dog off the leash. It needs to smell

