[SPEAKER_01]: that fire hydrant for a few extra minutes. That's okay. That's a beautiful analogy. I don't really want to corner you with the follow-up

20:07.175 --> 20:18.540
[SPEAKER_00]: question, Benjamin, but let's say some of us do not have that luxury of time. Because of course, if you are blessed enough to have unlimited

20:18.580 --> 20:25.686
[SPEAKER_00]: time or something, and I'm just putting it in my shoes, I'm putting myself in these shoes, that alright, I have this Paragliding Atlas

20:25.706 --> 20:33.551
[SPEAKER_00]: podcast project that I'm working on, and of course there are expectations versus reality. Is it 100 listeners? Is it 1,000? Is it

20:33.871 --> 20:42.858
[SPEAKER_00]: 10,000? Am I going to make it? Is the show going to be super successful? Or what's going to happen? Will it allow me to live my dreams? And then The

