[SPEAKER_00]: direction and then chase it through a hole. You just have to do some tweaks. So, of course, your kind of outlook works very well for people

21:18.010 --> 21:27.698
[SPEAKER_00]: who have the privilege. But for someone who might not be having that kind of luxury, what would you say how to navigate this as successfully as

21:27.738 --> 21:34.101
[SPEAKER_00]: possible without losing out too much on your goals? Okay, so I feel like we're almost having like a conversation of supply and demand here,

21:34.541 --> 21:43.364
[SPEAKER_01]: right? Where I could further elaborate into someone who might, look, let me give you a little bit more of a picture of who I have been so that,

21:43.884 --> 21:51.906
[SPEAKER_01]: because people might hear, how do you have three months to do this? How do you have five months to do that? So back in, it was 2008, right?

21:55.305 --> 22:05.758
[SPEAKER_01]: I had just flown a powered paraglider across Canada. I was making a film. It was like my first film about that. It's called The Canadian Dream. And

22:06.619 --> 22:15.585
[SPEAKER_01]: I wanted to do more of that. And I wanted to do it as... a free flying paraglider pilot. But I knew that I was going to have to invest a ton of

22:15.645 --> 22:22.410
